an Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 1","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Beginning at a point on line of mean high tide on north shore of Makushin Bay, Uhalaska Island, 53°45'31\" N. latitude, 166°55' W. longitude, as shown on U.S. Coast and Geodetic Survey Chart No. 8802.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 2","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Thence from said initial point, by metes and bounds,","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 3","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"North across Unalaska Island to line of mean high tide on Bering Sea;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 4","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Easterly and southwesterly around Cape Cheerful, Cape Kaletka, Erskine Point and Brundage Head along line of mean high tide with meanders of Bering Sea, Unalaska Bay, Kaletka Bay, Unalga Pass, Beaver Inlet, and Erskine Bay to the head of Erskine Bay;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 5","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p5","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Southwesterly on straight line across Unalaska Island to the head of Portage Bay at mean high tide;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 6","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p6","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Westerly and northwesterly along shore of Portage Bay and Makushin Bay at mean high tide around Cathedral Point to the point of beginning.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 7","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p7","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"The area described, including both public and non-public lands, aggregates 200,000 acres.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 8","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p8","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"All of Hog Island, in Unalaska Bay, near Unalaska Island, as shown on U.S. Coast and Geodetic Survey Chart No. 9007.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 9","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p9","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"The area described aggregates 110 acres.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 10","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p10","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"All of those portions of Unalaska Island, Umnak Island, and the small islands and rocks adjacent thereto, lying between 53°13'00'' and 53°35'00'' N. latitudes and 167°28'30\" and 168°6'00\" W. longitudes, as shown on U.S. Coast and Geodetic Survey Chart No. 8802.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 11","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p11","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"The areas described aggregate 148,000 acres.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 12","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p12","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Executive Order No. 8789 of June 14, 1941 reserving for the use of the War Department portions of the lands described herein as Tract No. 1 is hereby revoked.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 13","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p13","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"This order is confidential and shall not be published in the Federal Register, and shall not be made public in any other manner except upon prior authorization by the Secretary of War.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372517; common-crawl capture 2025-12-14T01:39:51Z; unnumbered paragraph 14","sha256":"b540ac41588a138caedca5199208997556dad5a6ce8ff087fcad631de05031cc","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9153-withdrawing-public-lands-for-use-the-war-department-for-military"},"scope_id":"EO:9153A#p14","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"11 FR 12839, PDF pages 1-3","sha256":"01fee856d33199b723de21503c2076d7ba98e5a2ba0b65e12078e07c92bf99ab","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1946-10-31/pdf/FR-1946-10-31.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 14 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_ord